From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: AltarsCN <337293323+Altars3668@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 30 Sep 2026 05:09:25 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] ntdll: Keep Unix names in UTF-8 in the C and POSIX locales.

Their charset is ASCII, which made every name beyond ASCII fail to
convert: PowerPoint could not save slides as PNG under a Chinese name
when Wine ran without LANG.  ASCII is part of UTF-8, so nothing that
worked changes.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>

diff --git a/dlls/ntdll/unix/env.c b/dlls/ntdll/unix/env.c
index bf1c816b1c3..019bfe2bf7a 100644
--- a/dlls/ntdll/unix/env.c
+++ b/dlls/ntdll/unix/env.c
@@ -218,7 +218,9 @@ static void init_unix_codepage(void) { }
 /* charset to codepage map, sorted by name */
 static const struct { const char *name; UINT cp; } charset_names[] =
 {
-    { "ANSIX341968", 20127 },
+    /* the C and POSIX locales' ASCII: names are kept in UTF-8, which ASCII is part of, rather than
+     * failing every name beyond ASCII */
+    { "ANSIX341968", CP_UTF8 },
     { "BIG5", 950 },
     { "BIG5HKSCS", 950 },
     { "CP1250", 1250 },
